course: dictionary
lesson: 12997
title: The word exposition
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Exposition is a long word, but it has a few simple meanings you can learn one at a time. It can mean a clear explanation of an idea, the beginning part of a story, or a big public show. Its short form is expo, so if you hear expo, think of a show.
explain: In a story, the exposition comes first. It introduces the characters, the setting and the background, so the reader knows who is in the story and where it happens. «The exposition showed Tom and his dog living in a small village by the sea.» After that, the story can start to build up.
explain: Use context to choose the right meaning. If the sentence is about a story, it means the beginning. If it is about explaining something clearly, it means an explanation. If it is about a big hall full of stalls, it means a show.
fact: Exposition means a clear and full explanation of an idea or subject.
fact: In a story, the exposition is the beginning: it introduces the characters, the setting and the background.
fact: Exposition can also mean a big public show or fair, often called an expo.
fact: In music, the exposition is the first part of a piece, where the main tunes are played.
fact: A story plan often has five stages: exposition, rising action, climax, falling action and resolution.
exercise: «The exposition at the start of the book told us about the castle.» What does exposition mean here? | The last page of the book | A loud noise in the night | *The beginning part of a story | A big public show
exercise: «Mrs Lee gave a clear exposition of how the heart pumps blood.» What does exposition mean here? | A big public show | A short and rude reply | *A clear and full explanation | The first part of a song
exercise: «The world exposition had stalls from forty countries.» What is a world exposition? | A story about the whole world | A school test | A type of music | *A big public show or fair
test: «The exposition of the song starts with a soft piano tune.» What does exposition mean in this sentence? | The final chorus | A big show with stalls | *The first part of a piece of music, where the main tunes are played | A clear explanation
test: Ella says expo means a big show. Is she right? | No, expo means a sad story | No, expo is only a music word | *Yes, expo is the short form of exposition, and it can mean a big show | Yes, but it means a short tune
exam: «Which part of a story introduces the characters and the setting?» | *Exposition | Resolution | Rising action | Climax
